WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.067
-Kevin, good to see you again.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.133
Danielle,
first time on our show.

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.601
-I know.
-You know, your --

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:06.801
your daughters weirdly
made a cameo on my show.

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:07.834
-Yes, they did.

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.200
-When we were
interviewing Kevin.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.667
During Zoom, they both just
hopped onto the camera,

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:14.200
if you can see them up there.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.434
-Oh, yeah.
There they are.

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:17.234
-Look at how cute.
So now I have the whole --

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:18.834
I've had --
I have your whole family.

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:20.167
-The whole crew
has been on the show now.

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:21.868
-On the show, yeah.
-They went on first.

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:23.667
-Yeah, I know.
-Yeah.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:24.968
Sorry about that.
-Was it fun

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:26.100
having them around
for interviews?

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.200
-Oh, you know,
they made it a game.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.067
They were like,
"I'm gonna make sure

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:33.067
that every interview is more
difficult than it needs to be."

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:34.801
-Yeah.
-But it was fun.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.267
It was a way for us
to bond as a family.

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:40.934
-Yeah. I heard that Questlove
D.J.'d your wedding.

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:42.167
Is that true?
-Yep.

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:44.367
-He did. Actually, I just
saw him at the Oscars.

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:45.701
And he -- and he said --

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:46.734
-You were great,
by the way, bud.

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:48.133
-Oh, thank you.
I had so much fun.

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:50.734
It was weird to be asked
to play for Reba McEntire,

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:51.834
and you're just like...
-What an honor.

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:53.434
-"Okay, yes."
You know?

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:55.267
-Yeah.
-And so, I actually called her.

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:58.133
I'm like, "So this weird thing
has happened."

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:00.667
It was wonderful, but then I saw
Questlove and his mother,

00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:02.334
which was awesome.
-I know, his mom...

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:04.200
-So nice.
And she was -- he told her

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.968
that, "This was my first
celebrity wedding I D.J.'d."

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:09.267
-Is that right?
-That's what he said.

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:11.000
Or D.J. gig.
I'm not sure if it was,

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.367
you know, wedding or D.J. gig.
-Yeah.

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:14.601
And how'd he do?
-He did great.

00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:15.701
-He crushed, right?
-I mean, there was a luge

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.434
in front of him,
and everybody was like --

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:18.667
-Yeah, everyone
had a great time.

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:20.567
No one ate the food.
-No.

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:21.634
[ Laughter ]
-No, of course not.

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:23.467
-So I billed it back to him.

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:25.167
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, yeah, any uneaten food --

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:27.167
Yeah, Questlove has to pay
for it if the D.J. is too good.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:28.534
-Too good.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:28.534 --> 00:01:29.968
You got to be a little bad
so you can finish the food.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:31.200
Yeah, exactly.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.534
Did he take any requests
from you?

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:35.667
-No requests.
-Yeah, me too. Yeah.

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:37.501
He sees me come up to the thing,
he's like, "Just go away.

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:38.667
Just go."
-"Get out of here."

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:40.300
-He's like,
"Please leave me alone." Yeah.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.834
-But then, you know what?
There was no requests needed.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.267
He was so unbelievable.
-Yeah, he's a great D.J.

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:45.501
I want to talk about this.

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:47.501
"There's a Rock Concert
in My Bedroom."

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:49.300
You guys wrote this great book.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:54.100
I have two little girls,
and I know you do, as well.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:57.934
Do they -- Do they perform?
Is this based on real lives?

00:01:57.934 --> 00:02:00.534
Do they want to sing?
Do they -- Do they get nervous?

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:03.501
-I think --
Well, Alena had this recital,

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:07.200
and she was practicing, like,
in the foyer for hours.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.968
And she was like -- I saw her
getting really frustrated.

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:11.934
-Yeah.
-So we'd turn on some music

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:13.767
for her, and we're like,
"Let's just have fun with it."

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.601
Like, "You -- You know this."
You know?

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:17.267
-Yeah.
-"You're just getting nervous."

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:19.267
And she ended up
having a lot of fun.

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:22.167
And then when she went on stage,
she remembered everything.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:23.701
So it was -- it was good.

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:26.634
What's good about the book is
that you can --

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:29.501
I feel like the girls
are so different

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:33.868
that when, like, one comes home,
I ask her, like, "How's school?"

00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:35.300
she's like, "It's great."
-Yeah.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.100
-The other one
doesn't say anything.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.534
-Yeah, she's like,
"I don't like school."

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:40.334
-She's like, "I -- I don't
really like talking about this.

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:42.200
I just like boys," you know?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.701
-Yeah, exactly.
-I'm dying inside.

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:45.467
-Yeah.
-But I feel like, then,

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:48.434
when I read a book to them and
I'm able to ask them questions,

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.801
they open up more.
-How old are they now?

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:52.767
-5 and 8.
-5 and 8. Yeah.

00:02:52.767 --> 00:02:54.234
It's the greatest.
That's --

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:56.534
My girls are like that, too.
And it's like, they're reading.

00:02:56.534 --> 00:02:57.968
And it's like --
to read a book to them,

00:02:57.968 --> 00:03:01.000
this is the perfect,
'cause my youngest one,

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.834
she sings songs in her --
in her bedroom and --

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:05.801
with her dolls and stuff.
And she's -- then I go like,

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:07.300
"Oh, sing me that song
you were just singing."

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.601
She goes, "I can't.
I have stage fright."

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:11.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:12.801
And I go,
"How do you know that word?"

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:14.234
-Yeah. Like,
"Where did that come from?"

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:15.534
-"What stage -- What stage
are you talking about?"

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:17.501
I go -- I'm not --
-"It's just my stage, Dad.

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:19.167
You just don't see it."
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:20.501
She's like --
And I'm like, I don't want

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:22.167
to pressure anything, you know,
because I would --

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:24.133
but I remember when I was a kid
and, you know,

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:26.067
performing at my parents'
parties or something like that,

00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:27.634
it's like, you get nervous.

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:28.767
But then,
once you get through it --

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.634
I mean, I'm used to it now.
And now --

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:32.567
Like, do you get nervous when --
-Oh, my God.

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:34.434
-Are you --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:35.734
Are you nervous now?

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:37.701
-There may have been some
tequila before we came out here.

00:03:37.701 --> 00:03:39.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:41.033
-Whatever, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:43.000
-Well, no, I mean --
but I mean -- to put you on --

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.300
'Cause you're like,
"My husband does that."

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:45.367
-Yeah.
-"I don't perform."

00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:46.868
-No.
-Yeah, no, 'cause my wife's

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:48.801
like, "Please. I can't even be
in front of the camera at all."

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:50.968
-She's so incredible, doing it.
-Yeah.

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:52.434
-It's just like --
it makes me so happy

00:03:52.434 --> 00:03:54.267
to be able to do stuff with her.
And, you know,

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.634
I have to deal
with these other two idiots.

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:57.734
-But that's why we were -- yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.734 --> 00:03:58.901
-How are --
How are your brothers?

00:03:58.901 --> 00:04:00.567
-They're good.
They're really, really busy.

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.534
And Joe was just here.
He did so good.

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:03.868
Well, actually, it was awesome.
-He crushed it, man.

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:05.868
He's so fun.
-He can sing his butt off.

00:04:05.868 --> 00:04:07.133
-I know.
You guys are great.

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:09.133
But I think this is a --
is a fun book, and I think it'll

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:11.400
build confidence
in any little kid out there.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.934
"There is a Rock Concert
in My Bedroom."

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:16.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:17.901
Thank you for coming on.
-Thank you.

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:19.434
-You nailed it.
Now I had the whole family on.

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:20.667
Come back, okay?
-Yeah!

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:22.634
-Kevin and Danielle Jonas.

00:04:22.634 --> 00:04:25.467
"There's a Rock Concert
in My Bedroom" is out now.

